Description: Serialize recipient publication while retaining reentrant notifications
 Guard receive-depth entry and pending-recipient publication with the same mutex,
 preventing another notifier from reading a vector while it is being modified.
 Use a recursive mutex because a registration callback can synchronously notify
 this transmitter. Receive callbacks still execute outside the mutex.
Author: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-20
